    "hash": "2828cc52cea1587dced2b58e8a2e4456b85a9669e1ce13a7263299880c6f9ccd",
    "summary_one_sentence": "After twenty years at war and adrift at sea, a traumatized King Odysseus washes ashore on Ithaca to find his kingdom overrun by hostile suitors and must reclaim his throne, wife, and son.",
    "summary_short": "Two decades after departing for the Trojan War, Odysseus washes up on the shores of Ithaca as a broken, unrecognizable wanderer haunted by the ghosts of his past. In his absence, a horde of ruthless suitors has occupied his palace, pressuring Queen Penelope to choose a new king while plotting against his grown son, Telemachus. To protect his family and restore order to his decaying realm, the reluctant monarch must shed his shame and embrace his inner warrior once more. Ultimately, Odysseus confronts the invaders in a bloody bid to reclaim his life and unite with his wife.",
    "summary_long": "Twenty years after leaving to fight in the Trojan War, King Odysseus washes ashore on his native island of Ithaca, physically battered and deeply traumatized by combat and loss. Disguising himself as a humble beggar, he observes his island in ruin and his palace overrun by arrogant, parasitic suitors vying for the crown. His devoted wife, Penelope, resists their aggressive demands for marriage by employing clever stalling tactics, while their son, Telemachus, struggles to maintain dignity and safety against assassination threats. Aided by loyal servants, Odysseus secretly reveals his identity to Telemachus, and together they devise a plan to end the suitors' tyrannical occupation. During a contest orchestrated by Penelope involving Odysseus's legendary hunting bow, the disguised king step forward when no suitor can string the weapon. Revealing his true self, Odysseus string the bow with ease and launches a relentless, brutal slaughter against the suitors trapped inside the great hall. Telemachus fights alongside his father, securing their victory and ending the years of terror that plagued Ithaca. With the suitors eliminated and peace restored, Odysseus and Penelope finally reconcile, coming to terms with two decades of grief and distance.",
    "synopsis": "An evocative, grounded retelling of the final chapters of Homer's epic poem The Odyssey, 'The Return' explores the visceral human cost of war and longing. Decades after departing for the Trojan War, King Odysseus returns to Ithaca not as a triumphant conqueror, but as a traumatized, solitary survivor. His kingdom has fallen into disarray, occupied by opportunistic suitors who demand Queen Penelope's hand in marriage and threaten the life of his young adult son, Telemachus. Hiding his identity under the guise of an impoverished wanderer, Odysseus must confront both the internal scars of his brutal past and the external forces threatening to eradicate his legacy before he can reclaim his home.",
